@startuml seq-tree
'' ============================================================================
'' vinary-viewer — Sequence: file-tree delivery, refresh-before-open, and scoped watching.
''
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the same directory has an initial-listing phase,
'' an async expansion gate, a retained watcher lifecycle, and explicit refresh
'' branches. `alt` and `== phase ==` keep those paths on one set of lifelines.
'' ============================================================================
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title File-tree — delivery, refresh-before-open, and expansion-scoped watch

autonumber "0:"

actor User #white
participant "main.service" as Svc MAIN_TINT
participant "git CLI" as Git FS_TINT
participant "main.dir-walk\n(fs)" as Walk FS_TINT
participant "Chokidar\n(depth 0)" as Watch FS_TINT
participant "preload `window.vv`" as Vv IPC_TINT
participant "re-frame\nevents/subs" as RF REFRAME_TINT
participant "app.db\n(:ui :projects /\n :ui :tree-filter)" as Db APPDB_TINT
participant "ui.tree\nfile-tree" as Tree RENDERER_TINT

== delivery (on open) ==
Svc -> Git : `rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n(cwd = file's dir)
Git --> Svc : repo root, or nothing

alt the file is inside a git repository
  Svc -> Git : `ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`\n(cwd = repo root)
  Git --> Svc : tracked & untracked-not-ignored paths
  Svc -> Git : `ls-files --deleted`
  Git --> Svc : tracked paths absent from worktree
  Svc -> Svc : subtract deleted paths
  Svc -> Svc : {root, files, synthetic?=**false**}
else no repo / git unavailable
  Svc -> Walk : adopt the containing directory\n(a directory is its own root;\na filesystem root is refused)
  Walk -> Walk : breadth-first walk, bounded\n(<latex>D \le 6</latex>, <latex>N \le 5000</latex>);\nskip dotted + heavy dirs;\nresolve symlinks, never descend them
  Walk --> Svc : {root=**realpath**'d, files,\nsynthetic?=**true**}
end

Svc -> Vv : `webContents.send`\n**vv:tree** {root, files, synthetic?}
Vv -> RF : `onTree` → dispatch `[:tree/received]`
RF -> Db : `projects/merge-project`\n(upsert by root; a covered synthetic\nroot MERGES into its coverer)
Db -> Tree : `:ui/projects` sub fires
Tree -> Tree : per project: `build-tree`\n(flat paths → nested map)\n→ collapsible `<details>` hiccup
Tree --> User : sidebar shows one controlled tree per project

== direct directory expansion ==
User -> Tree : click a closed `<summary>`
Tree -> Tree : prevent native toggle\n(render stays closed + busy)
Tree -> RF : `[:tree/expand root directory]`
RF -> Vv : invoke `vv:tree-refresh`
Vv -> Svc : validate offered + visible root\nand lexical containment
Svc -> Git : re-list repository
note right of Svc
  Synthetic roots use the bounded
  directory walk instead.
end note
Svc --> Vv : scoped {root, files, scope}
Vv --> RF : `[:tree/expand-ready]`
RF -> Db : replace subtree + add open scope\nin one event
Db -> Tree : render refreshed children `open`
Tree --> User : first expanded frame is fresh

== effective expansion watcher lifecycle ==
Tree -> RF : `[:tree/sync-expanded scopes]`
RF -> Vv : `syncTreeExpanded(scopes)`
Vv -> Svc : `vv:tree-expanded`
Svc -> Watch : reconcile one shallow watcher\nper effective [root, directory]
Watch --> Svc : add / unlink / addDir / unlinkDir\n(or `.gitignore` change)
Svc -> Svc : debounce + scoped re-list
Svc -> Vv : `vv:tree` {root, files, scope}
Vv -> RF : `[:tree/received]`
RF -> Db : exact subtree replacement
Db -> Tree : re-render expanded directory

alt collapse / ancestor collapse / Files unmount / project removal
  Tree -> RF : sync reduced effective scopes
  RF -> Vv : `syncTreeExpanded(reduced)`
  Vv -> Svc : release this window's ownership
  Svc -> Watch : close watcher when last owner leaves
else another window still owns the same scope
  Svc -> Watch : retain shared watcher
end

== explicit refresh ==
User -> Tree : right-click directory/project → Refresh
Tree -> RF : `[:tree/refresh {root, path}]`
RF -> Vv : invoke `vv:tree-refresh`
User -> Tree : right-click Files tab → Refresh All
Tree -> RF : `[:tree/refresh-all]`
RF -> Vv : invoke `vv:tree-refresh-all`
Vv -> Svc : re-list every visible offered root
Svc --> Vv : payload(s) through Promise reply
Vv --> RF : `[:tree/refresh-*-ready]`
RF -> Db : scoped/full replacement;\nremoved projects stay removed

== diff adoption (ADR-0038) ==
User -> Svc : `git diff | vv -t diff`\n(stdin spilled + typed, ADR-0036)
Svc -> Svc : open! → stdin doc →\n`send-stdin-diff-tree!`\n(effective kind = "diff";\ncommit diffs (`git-info`) skipped)
Svc -> Git : `rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n(cwd = the INVOKING dir,\n`doc-overrides/stdin-base-dir`)
Git --> Svc : repo root — else the\nADR-0036 skip stands (no tree)
Svc -> Vv : **vv:tree** {root, files, extras:\n[{path, name "**(piped diff)**",\nkind "diff", transient? **true**}]}
Vv -> RF : `[:tree/received]`

User -> Tree : open an on-disk `.patch`\n(stored outside its repo)
Tree -> RF : `:diff/render` resolves\nnavigable headers
RF -> Vv : invoke `vv:load-diff-sources`\n{diffPath, files, includePaths}
Vv -> Svc : resolve targets\n(diff's dir + ancestor walk)
Svc -> Git : `rev-parse --show-toplevel`\nper distinct target dir\n(short-circuit under found roots)
Git --> Svc : toplevels
Svc -> Svc : `dominant-root` (majority,\nfirst-seen tie-break) →\n`adopt-diff-project!` (guarded:\n`adopted-diff-roots`, repeat-free)
Svc -> Vv : **vv:tree** {root, files, extras:\n[{path, name = basename,\nkind "diff", transient? **false**}]}
Vv -> RF : `[:tree/received]`
RF -> Db : `merge-project` — extras **UNION**\n(dedupe by path, incoming wins;\nan extras-less refresh never wipes them)
Db -> Tree : extra pinned above the folders\n(italic `a.vv-file-extra`, opens like a file;\na diff INSIDE the root gets **no** extra row)
Tree --> User : the described repository is in Files\nwith the diff attached

note over Svc, RF
  Transient extras die with retention: `retention-fx`
  dispatches `[:tree/prune-extras]` at the same edge
  where main unlinks the stdin spill. On-disk extras
  persist — *Remove from Files* takes the project away.
end note

note over Svc, Walk
  Every local open sends a tree — a git root when there is one,
  else the containing directory as a **synthetic** root. Archive
  (`vv-archive://`) and remote (`ssh://`) URIs are excluded before
  `send-tree!` is reached, so they synthesize nothing.
end note

note over RF, Db
  A git root is a **fact**; a synthetic root is an **inference**.
  Containment therefore only ever removes synthetic roots: a repo
  nested inside a browsed directory stays its own project.
  A synthetic root covered by another does not duplicate it — its
  walked subtree is re-based and merged in, so the file you just
  opened is always in the tree (the `--others` invariant).
  A filter may force known paths open, but a direct-click scope that
  is still refreshing remains closed until its reply commits.
  Removal is manual — project header ⟶ *Remove from Files*.
end note

legend right
